<p>What follows is reproduced in John's own words, exactly as he wrote them: nothing edited, softened, or left out. Unlike his earlier books, this one carries no copyright date anywhere in its printing. The scanned file is dated February 2018, but that is only when it was scanned, not when it was written or printed. The book's own text gives a firmer date: the story "Curiodditie s" in Part Two opens "Most of this prattle is being written in February and March, 2001, to combat cabin fever," which places the book's writing, and so its printing, in 2001 or later. An earlier working note for this project had guessed "after 1997" from a different story's mention of a cousin's death that year; the 2001 date is what the book itself says and supersedes that guess. B &amp; B Printers of Gunnison, credited on earlier books, is not named anywhere in this one, though the "Hearty Salute to Thundermug" front-matter page below is addressed to a printing crew.</p>

<p>The book gives no table of contents and no chapter divisions of any kind; stories, poems, and pages of photographs simply follow one another, numbered on the book's own printed pages 1 through 24 (the book's page 1 carries no printed folio, but the numbering resumes visibly at page 2). For readability on the web it is split here into two parts of roughly equal length; the part numbers are this site's own division, not John's. Numbers in parentheses are the book's own printed page numbers. Ten of the book's twenty-eight PDF pages are given over entirely to photographs with no accompanying story text; where a page like that is reproduced here it is kept as one composite image rather than split into separate figures, so the original layout and captions stay together.</p>

<h2>Contents</h2>

<p>The book gives no table of contents of its own. The two parts below are this site's own division, with the stories, poems, and photograph pages each part contains.</p>

<p><strong><a href="/writings/hell-cats-and-she-ghosts/part-one/">Part One</a></strong> (pp. 2&ndash;13): Pink and Blue Booties; Snakes Alive; a page of family photographs at "the Ranch"; a page of Jackson family photographs, 1921&ndash;1945; Working Stiffs; Double Heart Failure; Hell Cats of a Different Breed; T-Bone; The Bullet Belt; The Lawbreakers; a page of World War II photographs; Hero For A Day; Hell Cats; Survival of the Fittest; Graveyard Poker; Ed and Cherokee; Curiodditie s.</p>

<p><strong><a href="/writings/hell-cats-and-she-ghosts/part-two/">Part Two</a></strong> (pp. 14&ndash;24): a reprinted newspaper article, "Mining Town Won't Quit," and a reprinted 1944 "Believe It Or Not" clipping; seven pages of "Favorite Photos"; Looking The Devil Right In The Eye; Short and Shorter; Conscience; and the closing essay, "Here's Laughing at You!"</p>

