<section class="source-doc-transcript">
  <h2 id="ode-to-lynn-key-lezotte">Ode To Lynn "Key" LeZotte</h2>

  <figure class="source-doc-image source-doc-image--compact">
    <img src="/images/site/hell-cats-lynn-lezotte.jpg" alt="Black and white photograph of an older man wearing glasses and a cap, laughing, head and shoulders only">
    <figcaption>Lynn "Key" LeZotte</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="source-doc-poem">
    <p>Hell Cats and She Ghosts, Lynn LeZotte knew them all<br>
    George Hatfield, Woody Wintz, Hank Slaght and Ray Ball<br>
    from the heavy spar mine at Wagon Wheel Gap to the Equity Mine,<br>
    far north on the map</p>

    <p>Muckers and miners, timbermen in the hole<br>
    Walter Waldo, Art Davis, Andy Prince and Bill Kroll<br>
    Lynn worked with the best and the best worked with Lynn<br>
    their red headed friend with the lopsided grin</p>

    <p>Mechanics and blacksmiths, ore sorters and flunkies<br>
    Al Birdsey, John Nelson and brave powder monkeys<br>
    Lynn learned from them and they learned from Lynn<br>
    from the Last Chance shaft to the Commodore bin</p>

    <p>Trammers and skinners and concentrates haulers<br>
    rough callused hands and grime on their collars<br>
    they bonded with Lynn, hard work was their lot<br>
    accepting the fate each working day brought</p>

    <p>Managers and shifters, bookkeepers, engineers<br>
    Erick Nelson, Bill Hayden, Henry Rowley, his peers<br>
    Lynn ranked with the best and the best knew that Lynn was the<br>
    heart of their mine with his lopsided grin</p>
  </div>

  <p class="source-doc-note"><em>Below the poem: "Appreciation: A sincere thank you to B &amp; B Printers of Gunnison, Colorado for its facilities and more especially to Jim and Kathy, thereof, who approach my ramblings with all the care of a crew cleaning up a hazardous waste spill. Their only stipulation being a three year &quot;cooling off&quot; period between manuscripts." This is the only place in the book naming B &amp; B Printers, who prepared John's earlier books.</em></p>
</section>

